<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Alpha-out curve for the CLOSE-exit of the platform's custom cross-Activity
     back animation.

     The Shell evaluates this resource with Animation#getTransformationAt(progress),
     which *does* apply the child interpolator (Animation.java: interpolatedTime =
     mInterpolator.getInterpolation(normalizedTime)) but never renormalises by the
     child duration. An interpolator is therefore the only supported way to make the
     closing page fade faster than the geometry clock. Shortening the alpha child
     duration would change nothing on the Shell path and would desynchronise the plain
     finish() window transition, which is driven by the same resource.

     Output y is the alpha interpolation fraction, so alpha = 1 - y. The curve reaches
     y = 1 at x = 0.60 and stays there, i.e. the closing page is gone after ~144 ms of
     the 240 ms post-commit clock.

     Before phase 2 this curve reached y = 1 at x = 0.26 of a 450 ms clock (~117 ms)
     and then held alpha 0 for ~333 ms while the window was still alive and still
     holding input. The absolute fade length is deliberately close to the old one
     (~144 ms vs ~117 ms, both far below the Shell's 450 ms reference); what changed is
     that the invisible remainder no longer takes three quarters of the clock.

     Measured through AnimationSet#getTransformationAt (the Shell's own path):
         progress   alpha
         0.02       0.949
         0.10       0.733
         0.20       0.482
         0.30       0.279
         0.40       0.130
         0.50       0.031
         0.60       0.000
     The 0.20 -> 0.40 band is where the closing page hands the screen to the already
     composed parent; below 0.10 the page is still essentially opaque, so a commit
     does not read as a flash.

     PathInterpolator contract (PathInterpolator#initPath): the path must start at
     (0,0), end at (1,1), and x must be monotonic. The cubic keeps x increasing
     (0.12 -> 0.28 -> 0.55) and y increasing, and the final horizontal segment keeps x
     increasing with y pinned at 1. Endpoints are exact so the shell's unclamped 0..1
     progress evaluates to alpha 1 at 0 and 0 at 1. -->
<pathInterpolator xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:pathData="M0,0 C0.12,0.30 0.28,0.86 0.55,1 C0.70,1 0.85,1 1,1" />
